--- !u!114 &361018062
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 361018061}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e8ea7bc5a80b1b54da0ca2178b6fd5f5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  DialogueOptions:
  - "\u201CI see you\u2019re not a local. Where are you from, and what brings you
    here?\u201D "
  - "\u201CThat must have been a hard journey. Was it worth it, now that you\u2019re
    here?\u201D  "
  - "\u201CSounds like you and the locals don\u2019t get along all too well.\u201D"
  AnswerOptions:
  - "<i>The immigrant walks in, his clothes and demeanor similar to that of a j\xEDbaro.
    He is slightly dirty, and his posture is stooped from a life of hard work. Despite
    this, he seems to be in relatively good spirits, and he sends a smile alongside
    a chirped, \u201CSalute!\u201D your way. </i> "
  - "\u201CI come from Corsica, a place you\u2019re no doubt unfamiliar with. I\u2019ve
    left a terrible war, and even more terrible living conditions to be here, as
    my family and I had heard there\u2019s work and land for those willing.\u201D "
  - "\"The locals mocked our accents, and haven\u2019t been all too friendly or seemed
    all that happy at our presence, but that\u2019s no issue of mine. The methods
    my people brought here have built <link=haciendas><color=#1A4D8F>haciendas</color></link>
    to rival any in the Caribbean. And for that, I think we\u2019re not doing too
    badly.\" "
  - "\u201CYou could say that. They think that we displaced them, I say we made their
    work easier. One thing is for sure, we\u2019ve definitely changed the way things
    work around here.\u201D"
  SourceBlurbs:
  - "Corsican immigrants fled due to growing political instability and economic hardship,
    looking for both land and opportunities in Puerto Rico where there was a quickly
    growing coffee industry (Pic\xF3, El Caf\xE9 y el Despegue, 1993). This was further
    encouraged within the Real C\xE9dula de Gracias (Royal Decree of Graces) - \u201CPero
    lo que vino \xE1 ser la verdadera aurora de nuestra riqueza material fu\xE9 la
    Real C\xE9dula de 10 de agosto de 1815. Esta c\xE9dula \u2026 decretando: la
    excensi\xF3n de diezmos y alcabalas, la libre introducci\xF3n de maquinarias,
    libre el comercio directo con la metr\xF3poli \u2026 permitiendo que los extranjeros
    pudieran establecerse en el pa\xEDs.\u201D {\u201CBut what truly became the dawn
    of our material wealth was the Royal Decree of August\u202F10, 1815. This decree
    \u2026 decreeing: exemption from tithes and alcabala duties, the free importation
    of machinery, free direct trade with the metropolis \u2026 allowing foreigners
    to establish themselves on the island.\u201D} [Real C\xE9dula de Gracias, 10
    August 1815, Bolet\xEDn Oficial de la Real Hacienda, Puerto Rico, 1815, https://enciclopediapr.org/content/real-cedula-de-gracia-1815/.]
    This decree encouraged European settlement in Puerto Rico by offering tax exemptions,
    free trade, and land rights. It directly facilitated the arrival of immigrant
    planters, especially Corsicans, who helped expand coffee cultivation, consolidate
    land, and shape the emerging system of agrarian capitalism on the island."
  - "While immigrants brought over a technical expertise that increased coffee production,
    they were often the victims of social marginalization and were forced to navigate
    the local labor hierarchies created by locals. Their presence changed rural communities
    and labor practices (Bergad, 1983; Pic\xF3, 1993)."
  - Both hiring and displacing local workers was commonplace at the time, changing
    preceding labor relations and therefore deepening social stratification as the
    immigrant planters became embroiled in the transatlantic coffee trade (Crist,
    Sugar Cane and Coffee II, 1948).
  AnswerVoiceClips: []
  PathingPoints: {fileID: 0}
  IsTalking: 0
  StopsToLookInWindow: 0
  StartingPosition: 2
  Name: Corsican Immigrant
  moveSpeed: 2
  exclamationMark: {fileID: 2017548017}
